{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310823,"nonce":"I6aX9UzanPmnYR/1fdVj/v3yzA4=","title":"BERT = Nue's second production architecture (user-directed 2026-07-14). Phased plan committed at docs/plans/BERT-phased-plan.md (1542e81e). ...","message":"**Directive:** pick up BERT next; Apple tools where available, portable approaches elsewhere\n(per [[feedback_nue_engine_flexibility]]). Plan of record: `docs/plans/BERT-phased-plan.md`\n(committed 1542e81e, 2026-07-14) — read it before starting any phase.\n\n**Phases (0→6):** golden fixtures (exact WordPiece ids + embedding cosine gates) → portable\npure-Haxe correctness on M1+NUC → embed-server + vector-search demo → AMX f16 reuse (encoder is\nall batch≥16, existing RZT_AMX_PREFILL route fits) → whole-encoder BNNSGraph mlmodelc per\nseq-bucket + first ANE numbers → NUC Q8/VNNI parity → per-model engine selector config.\n\n**Inventory surprise (verified):** `nue/arch/BertArch.hx` (143-line full builder),\n`transformer/{LayerNorm,MultiHeadAttention,GeluFFN,TransformerBlock}.hx`, and a 295-line\n`SafetensorsLoader.hx` + ONNXLoader all exist from the phase7-loaders era — registered in\nArchRegistry (\"bert\"→BertArch) but NEVER validated at model scale. Expect\nresolution-disease-class compiler findings when first exercised ([[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]]).\n\n**Missing:** WordPiece tokenizer (only BPE exists), pooling/embedding head, GGUF bert-arch\nmetadata keys, padding/attention masks.\n\n**Reference models:** all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (22M, primary), bge-small-en-v1.5 (33M),\nnomic-embed-text (stretch; rotary). Acceptance: tokenizer ids EXACT match; cosine ≥0.999 f32 /\n≥0.99 f16 / ≥0.985 int8; throughput = sentences/s @ seq=128 batch=32, cooled runs.\n\n**Why BERT loves our engine box:** encoder-only = every forward is prefill-shaped\n(compute-bound batch×seq), no KV cache/decode/causal mask → AMX/BNNSGraph sweet spot; fixed\nseq buckets suit CoreML artifacts; fp16 accumulation is fine when cosine similarity is the\nmetric. Whole-model graph → ComputeUnit=ALL = first ANE measurements.\n\n**PHASE 1 ENCODER DONE (2026-07-14, cosine 0.99999).** Pure-Haxe all-MiniLM-L6-v2 F32\nembeddings match the ONNX/sentence-transformers golden: cosine min 0.99999831 / mean 0.99999922\nover 32 sentences (fed golden ids; tokenizer separate). Commits: 19dc26af (Rust addInto\nbroadcast) + d77d8854 (Haxe encoder). Harness: `nue/examples/bert-embed` (static\n`BertEmbedder.goldenTest`). Run: `rayzor run Main.hx --no-cache -- \u003cf32.gguf\u003e \u003charness_ids.txt\u003e\n\u003cembeddings.f32.bin\u003e`.\n\n**What it took (all needed together):**\n- Correctness: post-norm TransformerBlock (BERT is POST-norm — pre-norm diverged every layer);\n  norm-name fallback (GGUF `attn_output_norm`/`layer_output_norm`); mandatory embed LayerNorm;\n  mean-pool+L2 head; bert `attention.layer_norm_epsilon`=1e-12.\n- **Two REAL infra bugs FIXED (llama never hit them):** (a) F32/F16/Q8_0 GGUF load didn't\n  orient dims to [out,in] like the quant path -\u003e token_embd loaded [384,30522], gatherRows read\n  wrong rows (GGUFLoader.orientDims). (b) addInto had no per-feature broadcast -\u003e [F] bias over\n  [seq,F] aborted; llama decodes seq=1 (numel matched) and is bias-free. Fixed in tensor.rs.\n- **Cross-module workarounds** ([[bugs_null_class_field_and_onearg_cast_xmodule]]): two-arg\n  `cast(x,BertModel)`, no Null\u003cclass\u003e fields (non-null+Bool flag), co-locate BertModel in\n  nue.arch, no mid-ctor optional params.\n- erf GELU NOT needed — tanh GELU passes (pool+L2 washes out the ~1e-3 delta).\n\n**PHASE 1 COMPLETE (2026-07-14) — end-to-end text→embedding matches sentence-transformers.**\n`BertEmbedder.embedText(text)` = WordPiece([CLS]…[SEP]) → encoder → mean-pool+L2. Validated on\nall 32 goldens from RAW TEXT (no golden ids): F32 cos min 0.9999983, F16 0.9999980, Q8_0\n0.9996910 — all match the Phase-0 quant-delta calibration. Commits: 54f02d0d/c6ed9004 (WordPiece\ntokenizer, 32/32 exact ids: GGUF uses ▁ word-start prefix not ##, + encodeUtf8 addChar), 779ad269\n(end-to-end embed + `embed`/`textgold` example modes). Run: `rayzor run\nnue/examples/bert-embed/Main.hx -- embed \u003cgguf\u003e \"text\"` (or `textgold`/`tok`/encoder-only).\n\n**3 native codegen bugs found + FIXED during bringup** (all at source, see\n[[bugs_native_codegen_continue_and_loop_output]]): array for-in + continue (46ccca49),\nArray\u003cInt\u003e.join SIGSEGV (c6441e35), raw Null\u003cprim\u003e operand in ==/!= i.e. inline Std.parseInt\n(1149054a).\n\n**Phase 1 loose ends DONE:** GGUFLoader.tokenizer widened to `Tokenizer` (b87378ad); attention-mask\nthreading — `Attention` interface + `forwardMasked`, additive −inf bias, maskTest PASS cosine 1.0\n(d50f3e00). The maskTest-in-loop \"SIGSEGV\" that blocked this was NOT a loop bug — it was an unfilled\noptional `?mask` arg reading garbage x2; root-fixed generally in build_call_direct\n([[bugs_optional_arg_unfilled_garbage_abi_slot]], commit 9a61251b).\n\n**PHASE 2 DONE (2026-07-15) — serving + demo, the product surface.** Branch `feat/bert-embed-server`.\n- `nue/examples/embed-server`: TCP server (sibling of llama-chat-server), loads BertEmbedder once,\n  request = newline-separated sentences (client half-closes write), response = `count dim\\n` +\n  one space-separated f32 vector/line. `bench_embed.sh` reports sentences/s + p50/p95 (cooled,\n  pkill hygiene). Exposed public `BertEmbedder.new/embedText/dimension()` for cross-module use.\n- `nue/examples/vector-search`: embeds a 14-doc corpus, cosine top-k. Retrieval correct: cats→cat\n  docs (0.58), moon→\"Apollo landed astronauts\" (0.70), deep-learning→\"neural networks/backprop\".\n- **Pure-Haxe F32 BASELINE (M1 Pro):** ~31 sent/s server-side encode, 41.9 smoke (short sents),\n  26.1 wall incl. per-request TCP+client; ~37 ms/sentence. This is the unbatched single-thread\n  floor — Phase 3 (AMX f16 ~2×), Phase 4 (BNNSGraph + ANE), and thread-parallel batch encode are\n  the named levers. TRUE pad-to-bucket batching deferred (encoder is single-seq; pairs with Phase 3).\n- **Found a general codegen bug** (orthogonal to BERT): Array.sort comparator that indexes another\n  array by its param panics (pointer-as-GEP-index) — [[bugs_array_sort_comparator_param_gep]];\n  demo uses manual top-k. Not yet fixed.\n**PHASE 3 DONE (2026-07-15) — AMX f16 fast path, commit 8488d48b.** Routed the plain-F32\ntranspose-B matmul through Accelerate's f16 BNNSMatMul (the same AMX engine the Q4 path used; only\nQ4_K_M reached AMX before, so BERT's F32 encoder GEMMs ran single-threaded NEON). `amx_matmul_t_f32`\n(quant.rs) mirrors `amx_prefill_matmul` but keys the leaked-once f16 weight cache off a plain-F32\nweight pointer (f32→f16, no dequant); grafted into `rayzor_tensor_matmul_t_threaded` — **the variant\nthe Haxe `matmulT` MIR wrapper actually routes to** (NOT the sequential `rayzor_tensor_matmul_t`; that\ncost a debugging detour). Gate = macOS + RZT_AMX_PREFILL on + m≥RZT_AMX_MIN_BATCH(16) + fully\nrow-contiguous. **~8× on a 40-tok sentence (12.1 vs 96.9 ms), ~1.6× on the mixed embed-server bench\n(50.9 vs 31 sent/s encode)** — win scales with seq len (short \u003c16-tok sentences skip AMX; true\npad-to-bucket batching would make every row eligible). Goldens hold at f16 gate: text cos 0.99999807\n(was 0.99999831 F32), mask PASS, tok 32/32; 51 rayzor-tensors tests pass. See\n[[project_untapped_compute_levers_apple]].\n**PAD-TO-THRESHOLD amplifier DONE (2026-07-15, commit 98ec1108).** `embedText` pads a sub-16-token\nsequence up to 16 with [PAD] + a mask that excludes it from attention/pool (bit-identical to unpadded\n— the maskTest invariant), so EVERY sentence's Linear GEMMs hit AMX instead of short ones falling to\nsingle-thread NEON. **embed-server encode 31 → 50.9 (AMX) → 166 sent/s (5.4× over pure-Haxe\nbaseline)**; p50 latency 224→104 ms. Goldens unchanged (0.99999807). Short sentences were the encode\nbottleneck; this was the single biggest realized throughput lever. Sequences already ≥16 keep the\nfast maskless path. (A lightweight per-sentence form of \"pad-to-bucket\"; TRUE multi-sentence batching\n— block-diagonal attention or per-seq attention loop over batched linears — would amortize per-forward\noverhead further but is a real encoder refactor.)\n- **NEXT:** Phase 4 (whole-encoder BNNSGraph mlprogram per seq-bucket + first ANE numbers), OR true\n  multi-sentence batching for more throughput, OR push/PR the branch (4 commits ahead of main).\n  Also open: [[bugs_array_sort_comparator_param_gep]] (vector-search uses manual top-k meanwhile).\n\n**Llama-track items parked meanwhile:** BNNSGraph per-shape prefill integration\n([[project_untapped_compute_levers_apple]]), legacy Q6 Rust fallback slowness, unpushed main.\n\n**Engine matrix (M1, ext-host context):** AMX-f16 default pipeline ~253 sent/s → **graph (RZT_EMBED_ENGINE=\ngraph) ~400 sent/s pipeline (1.6x)**, raw fused encoder 445-475 enc/s single-thread; **ANE (python CoreML,\nComputeUnit CPU_AND_NE): 967 enc/s raw — 2.2x the CPU graph**, cos_vs_cpu 0.999892 (proof it ran on ANE).\ntextgold with graph = **0.9999628** (fp16 whole-encoder vs F32 golden; gate was 0.99). NUC int8 = 127 sent/s\n(the x86 half). PIPELINE: bert_graph_author.py (python3.13 venv + coremltools 9 + gguf; scratchpad/mlvenv)\nauthors the WHOLE encoder stack as one mlprogram per bucket (128/256/512) with dims read from the gguf's\nbert.* metadata + weights baked from its tensors, validated vs a numpy ref (0.99993) BEFORE saving; artifacts\nnamed `\u003cgguf-stem\u003e.encoder_s{S}.mlmodelc` NEXT TO the gguf (model-generic — darmie caught the MiniLM-scoping);\n`xcrun coremlc compile` → BNNSGraphCompileFromFile_v2 (rayzor-tensors/src/bert_graph.rs, HANDLE-keyed\nregistry, hidden per-handle). Haxe: rayzor/ds/BertGraph.hx extern; BertEmbedder loads (dir+stem+dim) + pads\nto bucket w/ mask; BertModel.encode swaps the block loop for one graph call (bias -1e4 fp16-safe, NOT -1e30),\nfalls back on any rc≠0.\n**LANDMINES (all cost real time):** (1) a Rust binary calling BNNSGraph must link Accelerate EXPLICITLY —\nflat-namespace dynamic_lookup lazy-loads Accelerate's C++ statics mid-call → libc++abi typed-operator-new\nabort on macOS 26 (C probe with -framework Accelerate proved artifact+OS fine). (2) FFI symbols must be in\nrayzor-tensors' plugin_init SymbolEntry table (lib.rs) like every tensor kernel. (3) **NEVER string-concat an\nx-module extern's return** — Int return mistypes as object; `\"x=\" + handle` derefs the raw value via\nhaxe_std_string_ptr → SIGSEGV, and `:Int` annotation does NOT fix it (disease cluster). Compares/assigns are\nsafe. The engine itself worked FIRST TRY — both bring-up crashes were debug printlns. (4) mlprogram arg order\nis alphabetized — resolve by name (out, bias, h). (5) crash-report .ips (~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports)\nparse = fastest crash-frame source; stdout buffering eats printlns before a SIGSEGV.\nREMAINING for the ANE productization: BNNSGraph is CPU-only by design — in-process ANE needs the CoreML\nObjC/C API (or keep ANE via a python sidecar for batch); Phase 6 = engine selector config + second encoder +\ndocs/nue-engines.md.\n\nRZT_EMBED_ENGINE=ane runs the SAME mlmodelc artifacts on the Neural Engine from inside the rayzor process:\nsrc/coreml_shim.m (~90-line ObjC, cc+`-fobjc-arc` via build.rs, frameworks CoreML+Foundation; cc build-dep\nwas already in the lock) exposes rzt_coreml_{load,predict,free}; inputs = zero-copy external-data\nMLMultiArrays (strides in ELEMENTS); bert_graph registry stores Backend::{Bnns,CoreMl} per bucket, load\ntakes kind (0=BNNS-CPU, 1=CoreML CPU+NE), handle keyed (dir,stem,kind). Haxe env: \"graph\"|\"ane\".\n**FINAL MEASURED ENGINE MATRIX (M1, full pipeline, ext-host):** amx-f16 ~253 | graph ~400 | **ane ~830\nsent/s (3.3x amx, 2.1x graph)**; textgold cosines 0.9999980 / 0.9999628 / 0.9999443. NUC int8 127 (x86).\nIn-process beat the python projection (~700) — MLModel-from-ObjC skips coremltools marshaling. At ANE speed\nthe pipeline overhead (~0.4ms tokenize+embed+pool) is the next ceiling (~2500 sent/s cap) → the lever after\nPhase 6 = multi-sentence batching per graph call (the s256/512 buckets exist for it).\n\nEngine resolved AT LOAD per (platform × model): zero config default; NUE_ENGINE (legacy RZT_EMBED_ENGINE)\n= the single escape hatch; resolved engine echoed; hint printed when mac artifacts absent. **AUTO CHANGED\nBOTH DEFAULTS: Mac amx 253 → ane 830; NUC haxe 59 → int8 127.** All overrides verified both platforms\n(amx/haxe keep bit-class 0.999998; graph 0.9999628; ane 0.9999443; int8 0.9920855). int8 routes via\nSys.putEnv(\"NUE_INT8\") — env is process-global, x-module statics aren't. Selector lives INSIDE\nBertEmbedder's module — TWO new landmines: (1) a separate EngineSelector MODULE shifted function IDs and\nstartup landed on a PRE-EXISTING harmless trap stub (haxe.ds.TreeNode.new generic-compile failure's\nreflect-ctor wrap; baseline has the same 6 stubs uncalled — 410017 renumbering family). Debug flow that\ncracked it: exit 133=SIGTRAP → .ips crash frame → RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1 trap-stub list → BASELINE\nCOMPARISON (stubs identical, only callability changed). (2) sys.FileSystem pulls haxe.ds.BalancedTree\n(same TreeNode trap) and `catch (e:Dynamic)` pulls NativeStackTrace recursion → per-model .nue.toml\nDROPPED for pure detection (capability IS the per-model config — darmie's push). NUC needs\n`cargo build -p rayzor-tensors` for the .so whenever plugin symbols are added (stale .so = \"can't resolve\nsymbol\" at JIT link). docs/nue-engines.md has the matrix + recipe. REMAINING P6: second encoder\n(bge-class — needs a 2nd model gguf downloaded), then llama-prefill graph joins the selector.\n\nMerged the escape-analysis branch → main (FF, 10 commits) per darmie; all work now on main (ahead ~44,\nunpushed). bge-small-en-v1.5 (12 layers, CLS pooling — vs MiniLM 6L/mean) end-to-end with ONE addition:\nloader reads `bert.pooling_type` (1=mean 2=cls) → sets BertModel.clsPool POST-BUILD (field, not\nModelMetadata typedef surgery — x-module optional-field reads are a Null hazard); embed() takes [CLS] row\nwhen set. EVERYTHING ELSE GENERALIZED UNTOUCHED: same authoring script (12 layers from metadata, buckets\n0.9995-0.9998), same selector (auto per model per platform), same WordPiece/arch/engines. **MATRIX (zero\nconfig): MiniLM Mac ane 0.9999443 / NUC int8 0.9920855; bge Mac ane 0.9999792 / NUC int8 0.9982555; bge\namx (pure-Haxe 12L+CLS) 0.9999986.** bge goldens = sentence-transformers 5.6 BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5\nnormalize=true on the 32 golden sentences → nue/tests/bert/goldens/bge_embeddings.f32.bin; model+artifacts\nin ~/models/bge (Mac AND NUC). mlvenv now also has sentence-transformers (golden generation).\n**BERT plan: Phases 0-6 ALL DONE.** Next big levers: llama PREFILL fused graph joins the selector\n(2-block ANE probe designed — 2-4x ttft est.); multi-sentence batching per graph call (s256/512 buckets\nexist; pipeline overhead ~0.4ms/sentence is the ceiling at ANE speed); param-retention soundness bisect\n(gated off, RZT_PARAM_RETENTION=1 + RZT_DBG_RETENTION); other archs (Qwen2 near-free) + multimodal ViT\n(reuses BERT blocks).\n\nThe 2-block probe (llama_prefill_probe.py: real 1B Q4_K weights dequantized+f16-baked, RMSNorm+NEOX-RoPE-\nbaked-tables+GQA-tile+causal-const+SwiGLU, numpy-validated 0.999941): **CoreML CPU fused graph ~87ms per\n128-tok prefill (~1470 tok/s) vs current AMX/Q4 pipeline ~1.35s (~95 tok/s) = 15x.** ttft(128-prompt) would\ndrop ~1.5s → ~0.25s. The win is FUSION + pre-dequantized f16 (current path pays Q4_K dequant + per-op\ndispatch per matmul), NOT the ANE. **ANE REJECTED (ANECCompile FAILED) — bisected via STRIP=rope,tile,rms,\nsilu env: even fully BERT-shaped it fails → the DIMENSIONS (2048/8192/32h) exceed what stock mlprogram\nauthoring ANE-compiles (BERT 384/1536/12 compiles fine). Unlock = ane_transformers conv1x1 [B,C,1,S]\nre-authoring (big separate effort).** SDPA (iOS18 opset) didn't help ANE and REGRESSED CPU 11→22ms; best\nform = mb.linear + manual rank-3 attention (the BERT-proven pattern). FULL BUILD now justified: 16-block\ngraph w/ enumerated shapes (ONE ~2.5GB f16 artifact shared across buckets), outputs = final hidden + per-\nlayer KV (UMA zero-copy handoff to CPU decode), Haxe split = embed-lookup + lm_head + decode stay CPU.\nNEXT-ORDER (darmie: \"start in that order\"): 1) THIS full prefill graph, 2) multi-sentence batched encode,\n3) param-retention bisect, 4) Qwen2 + ViT multimodal.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_bert_second_architecture` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}